Pro is the early-access tier: the tuned, throughput-optimized versions of new platforms and scaling backends land here first, because each one carries a real hands-on support burden that is only guaranteed on the paid tier. The free build still [I]runs[/I] on Folia (basic regionized scheduling + async teleport) and supports cross-server moves via plugin-messaging (backends behind a proxy); Pro's tuned Folia adapter and durable (SQL/Redis) transports are what graduates to the free build once stabilized. Same configuration, same data files, same commands as the free build - [B]upgrade is drop-in.[/B]
 
[SIZE=2][I]* BungeeCord proxy adapter is planned; currently supported via plugin-messaging on the backend.[/I][/SIZE]
 
[CENTER][COLOR=#A0A0A0]------------------------------------------------------------[/COLOR][/CENTER]

[SIZE=6][B][COLOR=#27AE60]Built for[/COLOR][/B][/SIZE]
LeafRTP-Pro works on any server out of the box. It also shines for the setups that push the platform hardest - if any of these describe yours, it's the right tool:

[LIST]
[*][B]High-concurrency servers[/B] where /rtp spam used to spike MSPT and shake TPS.
[*][B]Folia deployments[/B] that need region-aware scheduling and zero foreign-region API hops in the teleport hot path.
[*][B]Multi-server networks (Velocity)[/B] that need cross-network LeafRTP with reservation tokens and shared state. Validated on the in-repo devstack: [B]2 Velocity proxies, 2 lobby servers, 2 backend servers[/B] behind a shared Redis transport.
[*][B]Large or pregenerated worlds[/B] where chunk-load cost dominates - the pre-validated queue and Anvil pre-filter pay for themselves on the first burst.
[*][B]Custom-generator worlds (Iris, Terra, datapacks)[/B] where the Anvil-first biome read keeps your safety config authoritative across MC upgrades.
[*][B]Operators of every stripe.[/B] Set it and forget it, or version-control your YAML and read the profiler - both paths work. In-game [I]/rtp menu[/I] is there when you want it; nothing is hidden behind it.
[/LIST]

[B]Platform requirements:[/B] Java 21+, on Paper / Folia / Spigot / Fabric / native NeoForge. Legacy Forge is not native - run the Spigot/Paper jar under Arclight / Mohist.

